     "type": "NUMERICAL",
     "marks": 15.0,
     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Industries (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  At the reporting date the carrying amount of a non-current asset of Coppervale Industries (CL) was Rs. 3,900,000. The recoverable amount of the asset, being its fair value less costs of disposal, was Rs. 3,760,000. An impairment loss of Rs. 140,000 had been recognised in an earlier year and had not been reversed.\n  During the year the recoverable amount of the asset improved to Rs. 3,810,000.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  An asset is impaired where its carrying amount exceeds its recoverable amount. The impairment loss is that excess. A reversal is recognised only to the extent the revised recoverable amount exceeds the carrying amount that would have existed had no impairment been recognised, and never beyond the original loss.\n\nRequired:\nDetermine whether the asset is impaired at the reporting date and calculate the impairment loss. Then calculate the reversal that may be recognised following the improvement in recoverable amount, and state the carrying amount after that reversal. Show all workings and state the limit on the reversal. (15 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
