     "marks": 10.0,
     "text": "The following facts relate to a transaction to which Thornbury Corporation (TL) is a party. Advise Thornbury Corporation (TL) on the position under the law applicable in Pakistan.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Thornbury Corporation (TL) and Glenmara Corporation (GL) entered into a partnership on 19 June 2026 without registering the firm, and the business was carried on under the name of Thornbury Corporation (TL).\n(b) Thornbury Corporation (TL) took goods on hire from Glenmara Corporation (GL) on 19 June 2026 and sold them without the consent of Glenmara Corporation (GL).\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing The Features of a Company, namely:\n(i) A sole trader is an individual who owns and runs his or her own business. The law does not recognize the business: the law recognizes only the individual who runs it.\n(ii) A partnership is a group of individuals who own and run their own business. Each partner usually contributes capital to the business. A partnership business is not recognised as a ‘person’ by the law.\n(iii) Unlike sole traders and Partnerships, a company is a legal person, separate from its owners. This is called doctrine of corporate personality i.e.\n\nRequired:\nIdentify the applicable requirements and explain how they apply to the matters described, stating any that do not apply and why. (10 marks)",
