     "text": "You are asked to advise on the following facts relating to Coppervale Enterprises (CL) and to the other persons named.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) On 12 May 2026, Coppervale Enterprises (CL) entered into a written agreement with Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) under which Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) was to supply goods to Coppervale Enterprises (CL) for Rs. 190,000.\n(b) A director of Coppervale Enterprises (CL) entered into a contract with Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) on 12 May 2026 under which the company was to purchase goods for Rs. 120,000. The contract was approved by the board without the director disclosing the interest.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Concept of Anti-Money Laundering, namely:\n(i) Money laundering is the illegal process of making amounts of money generated by a crime (called predicate offence), such as drug trafficking, terrorist funding or tax evasion, appear to have come from a legitimate source.\n(ii)  Example 01: A person is involved in money laundering if he has Rs. 5 million from smuggling and sale of illegal drugs and he represents this money as being earned from his legitimate business of trading in used cars.\n(iii) Money laundering and terrorist financing activities. Initially, AML laws were implemented only on financial institutions to control drug trafficking. Since then, AML and counter financing of terrorism (CFT) have become global concerns.\n\nRequired:\nSet out the requirements relevant to the matters above and the treatment that each requires, together with any disclosure the requirements oblige. (12 marks)",
