     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Corporation (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  During the year Coppervale Corporation (CL) supplied goods to Quarrystone Corporation (QL), an undertaking consolidated in the group accounts, at an invoiced price of Rs. 56,250. The price was at a profit of 50% on cost to Coppervale Corporation (CL). At the reporting date Quarrystone Corporation (QL) still held goods from this supply as inventory, at a cost to Quarrystone Corporation (QL) of Rs. 15,000; the remainder had been resold to third parties.\n  Coppervale Corporation (CL) holds 60 per cent of the share capital of Quarrystone Corporation (QL). At the reporting date Quarrystone Corporation (QL) owed Coppervale Corporation (CL) Rs. 24,750 in respect of the supply, the balance having been settled in cash during the year.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  On consolidation the intra-group sale is eliminated in full. The profit element of the invoiced price is therefore not income of the group. The profit attributable to the goods still held at the reporting date is UNREALISED and is eliminated as well, leaving inventory at cost. Intra-group balances are eliminated in full against the receivable or payable. Where the subsidiary is not wholly owned, the unrealised profit eliminated is allocated between the parent's interest and the non-controlling interest.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the cost to Coppervale Corporation (CL) of the goods supplied, the profit element of the invoiced price, and the portion of that profit that remains UNREALISED at the reporting date. Calculate the amount of the unrealised profit eliminated against the parent's 60% interest and against the non-controlling interest. Show all workings and identify the adjustment required to each of profit for the period, inventories, receivables and non-controlling interests. (15 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
