     "id": "pp-caf7-gen-2-q6",
     "number": 6,
     "section": "B",
     "type": "NUMERICAL",
     "marks": 10.0,
     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Consulting (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  Coppervale Consulting (CL) is financed by equity and debt. The market value of the equity is Rs. 43,000,000 and the after-tax cost of equity is 9%. The market value of the debt is Rs. 53,800,000 and the pre-tax cost of debt is 8%. Corporation tax is 30%. The company wishes to estimate its weighted average cost of capital.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  Post-tax cost of debt = Pre-tax cost of debt x (1 - tax rate). WACC = (Cost of equity x Weight of equity) + (Post-tax cost of debt x Weight of debt), where the weights are market-value weights.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the post-tax cost of debt, the weights of equity and debt on a market-value basis, and the weighted average cost of capital. Show all workings and state why market values are used rather than book values. (10 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
     "criteria": [
      {
       "id": "COMPUTES-1",
       "label": "Computes the post-tax cost of debt",
       "maxMarks": 2.0,
       "evidence": "numericLines",
       "errorType": "CALCULATION_ERROR",
       "terms": [],
       "rule": "verb:computes"
      },
      {
       "id": "COMPUTES-2",
       "label": "Computes market-value weights for equity and debt",
       "maxMarks": 2.0,
       "evidence": "numericLines",
       "errorType": "CALCULATION_ERROR",
       "terms": [],
       "rule": "verb:computes"
      },
      {
       "id": "COMPUTES-3",
       "label": "Computes the WACC as the weighted sum",
       "maxMarks": 3.0,
       "evidence": "numericLines",
       "errorType": "CALCULATION_ERROR",
       "terms": [],
       "rule": "verb:computes"
      },
      {
       "id": "EXPLAINS-1",
       "label": "Explains that weights are market values because WACC measures the cost of capital actually employed",
       "maxMarks": 1.5,
       "evidence": "reasonTerms",
       "errorType": "POOR_REASONING",
       "terms": [],
       "rule": "verb:explains"
      },
      {
       "id": "PRESENTS-1",
       "label": "Presents the workings",
       "maxMarks": 1.5,
       "evidence": "structureTerms",
       "errorType": "PRESENTATION_ERROR",
       "terms": [],
       "rule": "verb:presents"
      }
     ],
     "expectedAnswer": "Post-tax cost of debt 5.60%; WACC 7.11%.",
     "markingNote": "",
     "workings": "Post-tax cost of debt = 8% x (1 - 30%) = 5.60%\nTotal market value = 43,000,000 + 53,800,000 = Rs. 96,800,000\nWeight of equity = 43,000,000 / 96,800,000 = 44.421487603305785%\nWeight of debt = 53,800,000 / 96,800,000 = 55.578512396694215%\nWACC = (9% x 44.421487603305785%) + (5.60% x 55.578512396694215%) = 7.11%",
